  "releaseNotes": "NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.TONOASIS v2.0.5\n\nExplicit local TVM storage, mandatory shared private records and capability-aware bounded identity CQL. Native save/load/process reopen/query controls pass. Mongo/browser demo, signed public-network transport, NFT/wallet, CAS and full HyperDrive parity are not certified. See the provider README for current evidence.\n\nWhat's new since v2.0.4\n- Add native TON TVM contract proof and fix unsupported CQL capability reporting (0ea8699)\n- Add retained native TON and Mongo CQL browser demo with owned source evidence (fc62c5f)\n- Fix TON pacing after slow responses and preserve native HTTP500 gate (082506b)\n- Fix TON signed hash domain and verify recent CQL manager demo (de3e5ec)\n- Implement bounded TON CQL candidate with explicit native rate-limit gate (110364a)\n- Implement native TON snapshot ownership and encrypted C# storage backend (9bd26c8)\n- Record explicit local TVM native acceptance and fifth release readiness (ce07200)\n- Recover explicit local TON TVM source without changing legacy wrapper (2320ba7)\n- Replace TON EVM adapter with native private storage and bounded CQL (691c76e)\n- Validate exact TON masterchain header and zero-state contracts (fdb56c6)\n\nFull changelog\nhttps://github.com/NextGenSoftwareUK/OASIS/commits/master/Providers/Blockchain/NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.TONOASIS",
